+// TestCredentialPaths covers the review finding on credentials in the
+// paths of RZ-CFG-013 warnings (01 J row 013: the warning names the
+// detector, never the value; 01 req 48 and 49: the path is part of the
+// text and JSON forms): no warning shows the credential it detected, or
+// one an enclosing element names, in its path. Each row is one member of
+// the class, where the credential is a mapping key (in labels, in
+// annotations, in free content), a string set element, a key or string
+// of a composite set element, the key field of a keyed entry, or an
+// enclosing key or keyed entry of the warned value; the last rows show
+// the path keeps every element that shows no credential. want lists the
+// warnings' paths, sorted. An error below a credential (the RZ-CFG-011 of
+// a key holding ${) still names it by 01 req 48's path rule, which a
+// contract change request asks to extend to every diagnostic.
+func TestCredentialPaths(t *testing.T) {
+	const (
+		aws      = "AKIAABCDEFGHIJKLMNOP"
+		userinfo = "https://user:pass@example.com" //nolint:gosec // G101: a sample of the URL detector, not a credential.
